--- title Making a function from data
--- about MAKE FUNCTION! is what every other way of writing a function is
--- about built on. R3 defines FUNC, FUNCTION, USE, CLOSURE and DOES in
--- about REBOL on top of it, so an implementation that does not expose
--- about it cannot be extended with a new way of making functions
--- about without changing the implementation.

--- id making-functions/a-function-from-a-spec-and-a-body
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note The argument is one block holding two: the spec and the body.
--- code
f: make function! [[a] [a + 1]]
f 1
--- result
2

--- id making-functions/the-spec-it-was-given
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold spec-of make function! [[a] [a + 1]]
--- result
"[a]"

--- id making-functions/the-body-it-was-given
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold body-of make function! [[a] [a + 1]]
--- result
"[a + 1]"

--- id making-functions/a-function-of-no-arguments
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
f: make function! [[] [7]]
f
--- result
7

--- id making-functions/the-two-blocks-may-be-computed
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Which is the point of having it: the spec and body are data
--- note until this turns them into a function.
--- code
f: make function! reduce [[b] [b * 2]]
f 5
--- result
10

--- id making-functions/a-spec-with-no-body-is-refused
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
make function! [[a]]
--- error script bad-make-arg

--- id making-functions/two-things-that-are-not-blocks-are-refused
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
make function! [1 2]
--- error script bad-make-arg
